			"type": "text",
			"text": "Bulongosteus was a placoderm discovered in Junggar Basin of Xinjiang, a province in People's Republic of China, dating back to the Devonian. Its name is a reference to Bulonggor formation where it was found and the Greek word for bone. It had a head armor of about 18 centimeters, making it a small fish. This genus is important to science as its proof that placoderms could also survive in freshwater environments."
